{
  "title": "79: al-Naazea'at النازعات",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nوَالنّٰزِعٰتِ غَرْقًا ۙ‏(1)\nWAALNNAAZEA’AATE GHARQAN.\nBy the (angels) who tear out (the souls of the wicked) with violence; \nوَّالنّٰشِطٰتِ نَشْطًا ۙ‏(2)\nWWAALNNAASHETAATE NASHTAN.\nBy those who gently draw out (the souls of the blessed); \nوَّالسّٰبِحٰتِ سَبْحًا ۙ‏(3)\nWWAALSSAABEHAATE SABHAN.\nAnd by those who glide along (on errands of mercy), \nفَالسّٰبِقٰتِ سَبْقًا ۙ‏(4)\nFAALSSAABEQAATE SABQAN.\nThen press forward as in a race, \nفَالْمُدَبِّرٰتِ اَمْرًا‌ ۘ‏(5)\nFAL MUDABBERAATE AMRAN.\nThen arrange to do (the Commands of their Lord), \nيَوْمَ تَرْجُفُ الرَّاجِفَةُ ۙ‏(6)\nYAWMA TARJOFUL AR-RAAJEFATU.\nOne Day everything that can be in commotion will be in violent commotion, \nتَتْبَعُهَا الرَّادِفَةُ ؕ‏(7)\nTATBAU’UHAA AR-RAADEFATU.\nFollowed by oft-repeated (commotions): \nقُلُوْبٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ وَّاجِفَةٌ ۙ‏(8)\nQULOOBUN YAWMA-EZIN WWAAJEFATUN.\nHearts that Day will be in agitation; \nاَبْصَارُهَا خَاشِعَةٌ‌ ۘ‏(9)\nAABSAARUHAA KHAASHE-A’TUN.\nCast down will be (their owners') eyes. \nيَقُوْلُوْنَ ءَاِنَّا لَمَرْدُوْدُوْنَ فِى الْحَافِرَةِ ؕ‏(10)\nYAQOOLOONA A-INNAA LAMARDOODOONA FIL AL-HAAFERATE.\nThey say (now): “What! shall we indeed be returned to (our) former state? \nءَاِذَا كُنَّا عِظَامًا نَّخِرَةً ؕ‏(11)\nA-EZAA KUNNAA E’EZAAMAN NNAKHERATAN.\n“What! - when we shall have become rotten bones?” \nقَالُوْا تِلْكَ اِذًا كَرَّةٌ خَاسِرَةٌ‌ ۘ‏(12)\nQAALOO TILKA EZAL KARRATUN KHAASERATUN.\nThey say: “It would, in that case, be a return with loss!” \nفَاِنَّمَا هِىَ زَجْرَةٌ وَّاحِدَةٌ ۙ‏(13)\nFA-INNAMAA HEYA ZAJRATUN WWAAHEDATUN.\nBut verily, it will be but a single (Compelling) Cry, \nفَاِذَا هُمْ بِالسَّاهِرَةِ ؕ‏(14)\nFA-EZAA HUM BEALSSAAHERATE.\nWhen, behold, they will be in the (full) awakening (to Judgment). \nهَلْ اَتٰٮكَ حَدِيْثُ مُوْسٰى‌ۘ‏(15)\nHAL ATAAKA HADEESUL MOOSAA.\nHas the story of Moses reached thee? \nاِذْ نَادٰٮهُ رَبُّهٗ بِالْوَادِ الْمُقَدَّسِ طُوًى‌ۚ‏(16)\nIZ NAADAAHU RABBOHU BIL-WAADE AL-MUQADDASE TOOAA.\nBehold, thy Lord did call to him in the sacred valley of Tuwa:- \nاِذْهَبْ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ اِنَّهٗ طَغٰى ۖ‏(17)\nIZHAB ELAA FIR-A’WNA INNAHU TAGHAA.\n“Go thou to Pharaoh for he has indeed transgressed all bounds: \nفَقُلْ هَلْ لَّكَ اِلٰٓى اَنْ تَزَكّٰى ۙ‏(18)\nFAQUL HAL LAKA ELAA AN TAZAKKAA.\n“And say to him, 'Wouldst thou that thou shouldst be purified (from sin)? \nوَاَهْدِيَكَ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ فَتَخْشٰى‌ۚ‏(19)\nWAAHDEEKA ELAA RABBEKA FATAKHSHAA.\n“'And that I guide thee to thy Lord, so thou shouldst fear Him?'“ \nفَاَرٰٮهُ الْاٰيَةَ الْكُبْرٰى ۖ‏(20)\nFAARAAHU AL-AAAYATA KUBRAA.\nThen did (Moses) show him the Great Sign. \nفَكَذَّبَ وَعَصٰى ۖ‏(21)\nFA KAZZABA WAA’ASAA.\nBut (Pharaoh) rejected it and disobeyed (guidance); \nثُمَّ اَدْبَرَ يَسْعٰىۖ‏(22)\nSUMMA AADBARA YAS-A’A.\nFurther, he turned his back, striving hard (against Allah). \nفَحَشَرَ فَنَادٰىۖ‏(23)\nFAHASHARA FANAADAA.\nThen he collected (his men) and made a proclamation, \nفَقَالَ اَنَا رَبُّكُمُ الْاَعْلٰى ۖ‏(24)\nFAQAALA ANAA RABBUKUMU A-A’LAA.\nSaying, “I am your Lord, Most High”. \nفَاَخَذَهُ اللّٰهُ نَڪَالَ الْاٰخِرَةِ وَالْاُوْلٰى ؕ‏(25)\nFAAKHAZAHU LAAHO NAKAALA AAKHERATE WAL OOLAA.\nBut Allah did punish him, (and made an) example of him, - in the Hereafter, as in this life. \nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَعِبْرَةً لِّمَنْ يَّخْشٰىؕ‏(26)\nINNAL FEE ZAALEKA LAE’EBRATAN LEMAN YYAKHSHAA.\nVerily in this is an instructive warning for whosoever feareth (Allah). \nءَاَنْتُمْ اَشَدُّ خَلْقًا اَمِ السَّمَآءُ‌ ؕ بَنٰٮهَا‏(27)\nA-ANTUM ASHADDO KHALQAN AMIL SAMAAA-O BANAAHAA.\nWhat! Are ye the more difficult to create or the heaven (above)? (Allah) hath constructed it: \nرَفَعَ سَمْكَهَا فَسَوَّٮهَا ۙ‏(28)\nRAFAA’A SAMKAHAA FASAWHAA.\nOn high hath He raised its canopy, and He hath given it order and perfection. \nوَ اَغْطَشَ لَيْلَهَا وَاَخْرَجَ ضُحٰٮهَا‏(29)\nWA AAGHTASHA LAYLAHAA WA AKHRAJAL ZUHAAHAA.\nIts night doth He endow with darkness, and its splendour doth He bring out (with light). \nوَالْاَرْضَ بَعْدَ ذٰلِكَ دَحٰٮهَا ؕ‏(30)\nWAL ARZA BA’DA ZAALEKA DAHAAHAA.\nAnd the earth, moreover, hath He extended (to a wide expanse); \nاَخْرَجَ مِنْهَا مَآءَهَا وَمَرْعٰٮهَا‏(31)\nAKHRAJAL MINHAA MAAAHAA WAMARA’AAHAA.\nHe draweth out therefrom its moisture and its pasture; \nوَالْجِبَالَ اَرْسٰٮهَا ۙ‏(32)\nWA JEBAALA AARSAAHAA.\nAnd the mountains hath He firmly fixed;- \nمَتَاعًا لَّكُمْ وَلِاَنْعَامِكُمْؕ‏(33)\nMATAA-A’M LAKUM WA LE-ANA’AMEKUM.\nFor use and convenience to you and your cattle. \nفَاِذَا جَآءَتِ الطَّآمَّةُ الْكُبْرٰى ۖ‏(34)\nFA-EZAA JAAA-ATIS AT-TAAMMATU KUBRAA.\nTherefore, when there comes the great, overwhelming (Event), \nيَوْمَ يَتَذَكَّرُ الْاِنْسَانُ مَا سَعٰىۙ‏(35)\nYAWMA YATAZAKKARU INSAANO MAA SA-A’A.\nThe Day when man shall remember (all) that he strove for, \nوَبُرِّزَتِ الْجَحِيْمُ لِمَنْ يَّرٰى‏(36)\nWABURREZATE EZAL JAHEEMO LEMAN-Y YYARAA.\nAnd Hell-Fire shall be placed in full view for (all) to see, \nفَاَمَّا مَنْ طَغٰىۙ‏(37)\nFA-AMMAA MAN TAGHAA.\nThen, for such as had transgressed all bounds, \nوَاٰثَرَ الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا ۙ‏(38)\nWAASARA HAYAATAD DUNYAA.\nAnd had preferred the life of this world, \nفَاِنَّ الْجَحِيْمَ هِىَ الْمَاْوٰىؕ‏(39)\nFA-INNAL JAHEEM HEYA AL-MAAWAA.\nThe Abode will be Hell-Fire; \nوَاَمَّا مَنْ خَافَ مَقَامَ رَبِّهٖ وَ نَهَى النَّفْسَ عَنِ الْهَوٰىۙ‏(40)\nWA AMMAA MAN KHAAFA MAQAAMA RABBEHI WA NAHAA AN-NAFSA A’NIL AL-HAWAA.\nAnd for such as had entertained the fear of standing before their Lord's (tribunal) and had restrained (their) soul from lower desires, \nفَاِنَّ الْجَنَّةَ هِىَ الْمَاْوٰىؕ‏(41)\nFA-INNAL JANNATA HEYA AL-MAAWAA.\nTheir abode will be the Garden. \nيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ السَّاعَةِ اَيَّانَ مُرْسٰٮهَا ؕ‏(42)\nYAS-ALOONAKA A’NIL AS-SAAA’ATE AYYAANA MURSAAHAA.\nThey ask thee about the Hour, 'When will be its appointed time? \nفِيْمَ اَنْتَ مِنْ ذِكْرٰٮهَاؕ‏(43)\nFEEMA ANTA MIN ZEKRAAHAA.\nWherein art thou (concerned) with the declaration thereof? \nاِلٰى رَبِّكَ مُنْتَهٰٮهَاؕ‏(44)\nELAA RABBEKA MUNTAHAAHAA.\nWith thy Lord in the Limit fixed therefor. \nاِنَّمَاۤ اَنْتَ مُنْذِرُ مَنْ يَّخْشٰٮهَاؕ‏(45)\nINNAMAA ANTA MUNZERU MAN YYAKHSHAAHAA.\nThou art but a Warner for such as fear it. \nكَاَنَّهُمْ يَوْمَ يَرَوْنَهَا لَمْ يَلْبَثُوْۤا اِلَّا عَشِيَّةً اَوْ ضُحٰٮهَا‏(46)\nKA-ANNAHUM YAWMA YARAWNAHAA LAM YALBASOOA ILLAA A’ASHEETAN AW ZUHAAHAA.\nThe Day they see it, (It will be) as if they had tarried but a single evening, or (at most till) the following morn! ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Naazea’at (Those Who Pull Out)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 42 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the number of entities in the Heavens."
